# Network Components

#### Physical components like routers, switches, and servers work together with both wired and wireless connections to move data across networks.

#### These devices help direct, store, and manage information as it travels from one place to another. By coordinating how data packets are sent and received, network components make it possible for information to be transmitted quickly and reliably across the Internet - locally, nationally, and around the world.

<p align="center">
<img src="https://images.code.org/856b98a1b20b3c544923bc1736b8d759-Screenshot 2025-12-08 at 3.16.15 PM.png" alt="bits can be represented as 1 or 0" width="90%" style="border-radius:10px; border: 5px solid black;">
</p>

## 📝 To Do

#### Print the <a href='https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Lpw6E7-sh3it0ErJ9vcBdz7LiNpt4VQvOl73VPa55hI/edit?tab=t.0' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>AI Networks Chat Activity Guide</a> or *make a copy* of the <a href='https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1Q_TrOdI4yxGxOHlFstDs7nZIVDnbN9-Vqs_KIsPjQb8/copy' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>Digital Version</a>.

#### As you interact with the AI Chatbot on the next level, fill in the network diagram by: 
- #### Writing the function of each component in the network.
- #### Using arrows to illustrate the flow of data
	- #### Use dotted arrows for wireless communication
	- #### Use solid arrows for wired communication

#### There are some suggested chat prompts in the activity guide.

<br>

